# Run r1102, SQ-CDJ5 Boot 5: group B, fresh normal world cdj5b (README Boot 5: prep_srv.sh OUT cdj5b B spawn-animals=true;
# the Fungi cow / mooshroom counts need live animals). Worldgen counts are offline from the region files with
# tools/scratch_query/region_blocks.py (written for this run; it only reads). Shell steps run in OUT/srv.
# Order: SQ-MD-01 (Chunky 400 at spawn), then SQ-FGD-12 to -15 if time allows: five Chunky squares of radius 600
# (dark forest, swamp, mushroom fields, taiga, birch forest; about 5600 chunks each). Short on time: lower the radius
# in the SQ-FGD-12a..e rows to 300 and the 600s of the --box arithmetic in SQ-FGD-12 to -15 with it; say so in the run notes.
# r1102 run: radius lowered to 300 (disk 14 GB free); the --box arithmetic follows.
pace 2

## SQ-MD-01 | wild cave carrots: below Y 48, banded, never near the surface
bootexpect Done \(
bootexpect \[mushroom-spawns\] .*3 mod modifiers off
bootreject (?i)\b(error|exception)\b.*cave_carrots
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=cdj5bhome] run summon minecraft:marker ~ ~ ~ {Tags:["cdj5bhome"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=cdj5bhome,limit=1] Pos
capture S entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
> chunky world minecraft:overworld
> chunky center {S1} {S3}
> chunky radius 400
> chunky start
waitlog Task finished 3600
> save-all flush
waitlog Saved the game 300
shell python3 -I $INST/tools/scratch_query/region_blocks.py blocks cdj5b 'miners_delight:wild_cave_carrots$' --box {S1-400} {S3-400} {S1+400} {S3+400} --fail-above 48 --fail-depth-below 13 --json ../md01.json
look rows/SQ-MD-01.shell.txt: Y bands -24..23 about twice 24..47 and -64..-25, all non-zero; biomes spread; noise and carver caves both (judge a few spots with /zq count, or leave to the client tour). The 2026-11-01 instance log said "2 mod modifiers off": a 3 here means the Miner's cave_carrots modifier is the third

