## SQ-FGD-12 | surface Fungi mushrooms by biome (offline)
shell for b in "DF {DF1} {DF3}" "SW {SW1} {SW3}" "MF {MF1} {MF3}" "TA {TA1} {TA3}" "BI {BI1} {BI3}"; do set -- $b; echo "== $1 square"; python3 -I $INST/tools/scratch_query/region_blocks.py blocks cdj5b '(fungidelight:(inky_cap|morel)_mushroom|minecraft:(brown|red)_mushroom)$' --box $(($2-300)) $(($3-300)) $(($2+300)) $(($3+300)) --json ../fgd12_$1_singles.json; python3 -I $INST/tools/scratch_query/region_blocks.py blocks cdj5b 'fungidelight:(inky_cap|morel)_mushroom_block$' --box $(($2-300)) $(($3-300)) $(($2+300)) $(($3+300)); python3 -I $INST/tools/scratch_query/region_blocks.py blocks cdj5b 'fungidelight:[a-z_]+_colony$' --near 'minecraft:(dirt|coarse_dirt|podzol|rooted_dirt|grass_block|mycelium|moss_block)$' --box $(($2-300)) $(($3-300)) $(($2+300)) $(($3+300)); done
look rows/SQ-FGD-12.shell.txt (depth 0..1 = surface): inky cap only in dark forest and mushroom fields at the surface, morel also in the swamp; none at the surface in taiga or birch; dark-forest Fungi singles clearly rarer than brown / red; mushroom fields: huge inky in about 1 of 3 chunks, huge morel 1 of 4 ("chunks with a match by surface biome"); colonies next to dirt / podzol

## SQ-FGD-13 | underground Fungi mushrooms (offline, same squares)
shell for b in "DF {DF1} {DF3}" "SW {SW1} {SW3}" "MF {MF1} {MF3}" "TA {TA1} {TA3}" "BI {BI1} {BI3}"; do set -- $b; echo "== $1 square"; python3 -I $INST/tools/scratch_query/region_blocks.py blocks cdj5b 'fungidelight:(inky_cap|morel)_mushroom$' --near 'minecraft:(stone|deepslate|tuff|sculk|dirt|rooted_dirt|moss_block)$' --box $(($2-300)) $(($3-300)) $(($2+300)) $(($3+300)); python3 -I $INST/tools/scratch_query/region_blocks.py blocks cdj5b '(fungidelight:[a-z_]+_colony|farmersdelight:(brown|red)_mushroom_colony)$' --near 'minecraft:(stone|deepslate|tuff|andesite|diorite|granite)$' --box $(($2-300)) $(($3-300)) $(($2+300)) $(($3+300)); done
look below Y 50 and depth 13+: inky and morel singles rare, on stone / sculk / dirt floors; colonies of all four only over dirt-type blocks (a stone neighbour count near the colony total = colonies on bare stone: FAIL); none under open sky. A load error naming environment_scan or surface_relative_threshold_filter: grep latest.log

## SQ-FGD-14 | rooted dirt and truffle dirt (offline)
bootreject (?i)\b(error|exception)\b.*(truffle_dirt|rooted_dirt|wild_crops)
shell for b in "DF {DF1} {DF3}" "TA {TA1} {TA3}" "BI {BI1} {BI3}" "SW {SW1} {SW3}"; do set -- $b; echo "== $1 square"; python3 -I $INST/tools/scratch_query/region_blocks.py blocks cdj5b 'minecraft:rooted_dirt$' --box $(($2-300)) $(($3-300)) $(($2+300)) $(($3+300)); python3 -I $INST/tools/scratch_query/region_blocks.py blocks cdj5b 'fungidelight:truffle_dirt$' --near 'minecraft:rooted_dirt$' --box $(($2-300)) $(($3-300)) $(($2+300)) $(($3+300)); done
look both near the surface in dark forest and cold forest (taiga, grove) biomes, none in a conifer biome that is neither (read the by_biome lines; the four squares hold several biomes each, e.g. old growth or windswept forests); truffle dirt mostly with a rooted dirt neighbour. Rooted dirt but no truffle dirt: the two rules ran in the wrong order (merge them, row text)

## SQ-FGD-15 | mooshroom colours and Fungi cows by biome; summoned and egg mooshrooms red
shell for b in "DF {DF1} {DF3}" "SW {SW1} {SW3}" "MF {MF1} {MF3}" "TA {TA1} {TA3}" "BI {BI1} {BI3}"; do set -- $b; echo "== $1 square"; python3 -I $INST/tools/scratch_query/region_blocks.py entities cdj5b '^(minecraft:mooshroom|fungidelight:[a-z_]+_cow)$' --field Type --box $(($2-300)) $(($3-300)) $(($2+300)) $(($3+300)); done
pace 0.2
repeat 20
> summon minecraft:mooshroom {S1} {S2} {S3} {Tags:["fgd15s"]}
end
pace 2
sleep 2
> execute as @e[type=minecraft:mooshroom,tag=fgd15s,nbt={Type:"red"}] run say FGD15 summoned red
> execute as @e[type=minecraft:mooshroom,tag=fgd15s,nbt={Type:"brown"}] run say FGD15 summoned brown
count FGD15 summoned red == 20
reject FGD15 summoned brown
> fill {S1+5} {S2-1} {S3-1} {S1+7} {S2-1} {S3+1} minecraft:stone
> fill {S1+5} {S2} {S3-1} {S1+7} {S2+3} {S3+1} minecraft:air
> pbot spawn egg {S1+3} {S2} {S3} minecraft:overworld survival
> pbot hold egg minecraft:mooshroom_spawn_egg 20
pace 0.5
repeat 20
> pbot use egg {S1+6} {S2-1} {S3} up
end
pace 2
sleep 2
> execute positioned {S1+6} {S2} {S3} as @e[type=minecraft:mooshroom,distance=..8,tag=!fgd15s,nbt={Type:"red"}] run say FGD15 egg red
> execute positioned {S1+6} {S2} {S3} as @e[type=minecraft:mooshroom,distance=..8,tag=!fgd15s,nbt={Type:"brown"}] run say FGD15 egg brown
count FGD15 egg red == 20
reject FGD15 egg brown
look entity census (rows/SQ-FGD-15.shell.txt): dark forest about 50 % brown, mushroom fields about 25 %, at least 20 mooshrooms per sample; Fungi cows rare in dark forest, morel cows in swamps, both common in mushroom fields. Too few mooshrooms per square: record (chunk-generation spawns are sparse in this pack, gotchas.md)
